/*  modSeamT -- THE MODIFIER SEAM, TWO SCAFFOLD ROOTS, BOTH ROADS.

    Commissioned by Tony, SEQ 192, 2026-09-22. The question is whether a term's
    MODIFIER survives generation, and the instrument is THE CURSOR, not the
    verdict -- a parse that dropped a modifier can still report WIN.

    THE TWO ROOTS, and they are the smallest steppable thing:
        optT isRule "a"- "b"?- ;      drive optT("a")     does the ? survive
        repT isRule "a"+ ;            drive repT("aaa")   how many does it consume

    NO CODE BODIES, DELIBERATELY. An earlier cut gave each root a code={} marker
    for its verdict; the body is PARSED INSIDE THE DRIVE on first fire, which
    walks the mark out of the drive string and destroys the very reading this
    fixture exists to take. The verdict observable is `CAPFIRE fireLabelMethod
    <rule>`, which prints on both roads and ONLY on success -- fireLabelMethod is
    reached under `if sukcess` in parse() and in exitFromParse alike -- so no
    action is needed for it.

    THE CURSOR OBSERVABLE IS `MARKPT 2b-before-pop`, paired with `MARKARM drive
    base=`. MARKARM records the drive string's base and length at push; 2b reads
    atRuleMark immediately before the divert pops, which is the last instant the
    drive's own cursor exists. Both are parseTrace-gated and both fire on BOTH
    ROADS, which is what makes this a two-road comparison rather than two
    separate measurements.
    ⚠ CONSUMED IS AN OFFSET, NOT AN ADDRESS -- `mark - base` -- because the
    addresses move every run under ASLR and a pinned address would be rule H3's
    exact prohibition: an assertion that moves for reasons unrelated to
    correctness. The `in=` field carries the other half: DRIVE-STRING means the
    mark is still inside the drive, not-in-drive means it left it entirely.

    ⚠⚠ MS-5 IS TERMINAL AND EVERYTHING BELOW IT IS UNREACHABLE. `repT("aaa")` on
    the OLD road EXITS 139 -- `GroupItem::getText()` on a null `this`,
    GroupItem.mm:1322, reached through `ACTFIRE fireLabelMethod GrouP`. So the
    sentinel and the MS-6/MS-7 rows cannot be reached, and they are pinned
    UNREACHABLE rather than pinned to a value: a row behind a crash asserts
    nothing, and pinning it to its absent reading would be an absence check
    wearing a diff's clothes.
    ⚠ MEASURED PRE-EXISTING, NOT CAUSED BY SEQ 191. Built at b5e1557 -- the seal
    immediately before the attachLabel conversion -- and `repT("aaa")` exits 139
    there too, with optT's four cells reading identically. The control was run
    because SEQ 191's identity guard sits immediately above attachLabel's
    labelled-repetition branch, which is exactly this shape.
    ⚠ AND THE OLD-ROAD DRIVE MUST COME FIRST OR IT IS NOT THE OLD ROAD, so the
    ordering is forced: parser() is a one-way door. repT's generated body and its
    new-road cursor reading therefore CANNOT live in this file beside its
    old-road drive. They are measured in tester, which Tony steps.

    ROWS
      MS-1  optT OLD   verdict WIN, mark leaves the drive string      pinned
      MS-3  optT NEW   verdict WIN, and CONSUMED 0                    born red
      MS-5  repT OLD   exit 139                                       pinned as the defect
      MS-6  repT NEW   unreachable
      SENT  unreachable

    ⚠ NEITHER GENERATED BODY IS ASSERTED HERE, AND THE REASON IS THE TRUNCATION
    RATHER THAN A CHOICE. generateParse prints the body to cout, which is block
    buffered and flushed at exit; MS-5 crashes before that flush, so NO body
    reaches this file's capture at all -- optT's included, even though optT was
    generated long before the crash. A row greping for it could only ever fail.
    The bodies are read in tester, which stops cleanly, and they are:
        optT = CodE { return GrouP() && GrouP(); }
        repT = CodE { return GrouP(); }
    Do not add a body row here until MS-5 stops crashing.

    ⚠ MS-3 IS THE WHOLE POINT AND IT IS THE ANTI-VACUITY PAIR TO MS-1. Both roads
    say WIN. Only the cursor separates them, and it separates them completely:
    old road leaves the drive string, new road has not moved off its base. A
    fixture that read the verdict alone would be green on both and would be
    measuring nothing.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities list;
define
    optT isRule "a"- "b"?- ;
    repT isRule "a"+ ;
    msOptOld code={ cerr "MS-1 optT OLD":; traceParse("on"); optT("a"); traceParse("off"); cerr "MS-1-BACK":; };
    msOptNew code={ cerr "MS-3 optT NEW":; traceParse("on"); optT("a"); traceParse("off"); cerr "MS-3-BACK":; };
    msRepOld code={ cerr "MS-5 repT OLD":; traceParse("on"); repT("aaa"); traceParse("off"); cerr "MS-5-BACK":; };
    msRepNew code={ cerr "MS-7 repT NEW":; traceParse("on"); repT("aaa"); traceParse("off"); cerr "MS-7-BACK":; };
    ;
msOptOld();
cerr "MS-2 generate optT":;
parser(optT);
msOptNew();
msRepOld();
cerr "MS-6 generate repT":;
parser(repT);
msRepNew();
cerr "MODSEAM SENTINEL":;
stop();
